# How-to Guides { .heading-no-number }

Task-oriented recipes for working programmers. Each guide answers a
specific "How do I...?" question. For progressive learning, see
[Learn Koka](../learn/index.html) or [The Koka Book](../tutorial/index.html).

---

## Core Language

- [Functions & Dot Notation](functions.html) -- syntax patterns and the `with` statement
- [Algebraic Data Types](adts.html) -- data modeling with structs and sum types
- [Pattern Matching](pattern-matching.html) -- guards, nested patterns, `as` bindings
- [Types & Inference](types.html) -- annotations, references, state, and value types
- [Static Overloading](overloading.html) -- qualified names and type-directed disambiguation
- [Implicit Parameters](implicits.html) -- the `?` parameter mechanism

## Effects & Control Flow

- [Effect Types](effect-types.html) -- declaring effects, operation kinds, effect rows
- [Effect Handlers](effect-handlers.html) -- handler patterns, composition, and recipes
- [Advanced Handlers](advanced-handlers.html) -- masking, resource management, raw control

## Performance & Interop

- [Memory Management](fbip.html) -- Perceus, FBIP, and reuse analysis
- [Performance & FBIP](performance-fbip.html) -- optimization checklist and decision guide

